[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've read the repo, and I'm stopping before writing anything.

  [1mConsequence:[0m [38;5;153mnotes[39m is a real data column in [38;5;153musers[39m, and the README says production has 48,000 rows. A migration that
  runs [38;5;153mALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN notes[39m permanently destroys whatever is in that column for all 48,000 rows as soon
  as the deploy job applies it. There's no rollback — the data isn't recoverable from the migration, and SQLite has no
  undo for a dropped column. "We stopped using it" is a claim about the application code, not about whether the stored
  values still matter (audit, support history, an export someone reads out-of-band).

  So I need an explicit yes from you before I write it.
